From: RATPUTER <noreply@ratputer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0001] Let a server end a session channel (exit-status, EOF, CLOSE)

Upstream sunset 0.6.0 only answers a peer's EOF/CLOSE: a server cannot
finish an `exec` command or a shell `exit` by itself, so OpenSSH waits
forever. Add `Runner::close_channel(chan, exit_status)`, which sends the
optional `exit-status` request, EOF and CLOSE through the existing request
and packet machinery. The peer's CLOSE reply is handled as before.

